 will see the key already exists with revision 1 and expected 0, causing a conflict.\n\nI should also verify that a brand new key with a nonzero expected revision correctly fails, since an absent key implicitly has revision 0 — my `!exists && expected != 0` conflict check handles that case. Now I'm looking at whether the `Update` test in api.go passes a context argument to match the function signature.\n\nWriting wrapper functions...\n\nSince Snapshot already returns a copy, I can simplify replica.Copy to just return that copy directly, since the test deletes from the returned map and expects the store to be unaffected.\n\nNow checking the context cancellation timing: the test cancels immediately then expects Put and Get to behave correctly. My implementation checks ctx.Err() before acquiring the lock, which handles this case fine, so I don't need an extra check inside the lock for the tests to pass.\n\nWriting the Put method with validation and conflict checks...\n\nThis logic handles all the test cases correctly, so now I'll move on to writing out the complete files.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":119,"cache_read_input_tokens":15204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":119},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99617e4d-79ea-458e-aa12-0f920a72ef07","uuid":"53dc52e7-04e5-4448-b185-b6440414b1a5"}
